menu "Audio playback (drivers/audio_playback)"

    config AUDIO_PLAYBACK_DMA_FRAME_MS
        int "Default milliseconds of audio per DMA descriptor"
        default 2
        range 1 20
        help
            Lower means lower output latency and more interrupts. One descriptor
            must stay under 4092 bytes, which audio_playback_init() enforces: at
            48 kHz stereo 32-bit that is 5 ms.

    config AUDIO_PLAYBACK_DMA_FRAME_COUNT
        int "Default DMA descriptor count"
        default 4
        range 2 16
        help
            Total DMA buffering is FRAME_MS x FRAME_COUNT, and is the slack the
            playback task has to refill after a late wake-up. Two is the minimum
            for double-buffering (FW-AUD-032).

    config AUDIO_PLAYBACK_PREFILL_MS
        int "Default prefill depth (ms)"
        default 10
        range 0 500
        help
            Audio that must accumulate in the source ring before playback starts,
            and again after a complete starvation. This is the hysteresis that
            stops a source running at exactly nominal rate from clicking once per
            DMA frame. It adds directly to output latency, so keep it near the
            worst-case jitter of whoever writes the ring — a USB OUT stream needs
            about one frame plus host jitter. Zero disables the hysteresis and is
            only sensible when the writer is known to run ahead.

    config AUDIO_PLAYBACK_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Playback task priority"
        default 19
        range 1 24
        help
            Below audio_capture (20), whose losses are irrecoverable, and above
            every application task. A missed playback frame is an audible click,
            not lost data, and the DMA chain covers FRAME_MS x FRAME_COUNT of
            lateness (SDD §8.1).

    config AUDIO_PLAYBACK_TASK_CORE
        int "Playback task core affinity"
        default 1
        range 0 1
        help
            Core 1, away from the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth stacks on core 0 (ADR-009).

    config AUDIO_PLAYBACK_TASK_STACK
        int "Playback task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384

endmenu
